#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124115 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Two-Variable Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "35a664b8-a895-5c52-a92f-b62c75b44744" :question/math-academy-id "e-11026" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ given that $f(x,y) = 3x\\ln y + 2ye^x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+2{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124119 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59c3f441-0499-575c-af10-b597d61e6e35" :knowledge-point/title "Partial Derivatives as Limits of Difference Quotients"}] :question/id #uuid "a14d53ae-1922-531d-bb2a-bda9b4829f6e" :question/math-academy-id "e-11045" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y) = y^2\\ln{x},$ express $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\left(\\dfrac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x) = y^2 \\ln{x},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y) = y^2\\ln(x+h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0}\\left( \\dfrac{y^2\\ln(x+h) -y^2\\ln{x} }{h}\\right).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124120 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "ee2294e1-1e9a-5be5-be47-4c2e295b640a" :question/math-academy-id "e-11049" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) = x^2y^2+\\sin{x}\\cos{y},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,2\\pi )} & =2\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\pi )^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 4{\\pi }^{2}+(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8{\\pi }^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59c3f441-0499-575c-af10-b597d61e6e35" :knowledge-point/title "Partial Derivatives as Limits of Difference Quotients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d9bfc85-61f7-5d83-90bb-46d038a2035a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}+{2}^{x+2y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316566} {:answer/id #uuid "16d54e95-cdf6-5489-8299-3f1ac6a101a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{xh+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316567} {:answer/id #uuid "ef83f2da-4fa8-52eb-9e32-4c1e5415c956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316568} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b6a54f-2a86-5e16-af0f-f2eab80158c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+2h+2y}-{2}^{x+2yy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316569} {:answer/id #uuid "32295375-f7b2-5f17-a00d-1e854426090d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{xh+2y}+{2}^{x+2y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef83f2da-4fa8-52eb-9e32-4c1e5415c956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316568} :answer-field/id #uuid "56106e46-cc12-55ae-9c18-c51a81edefc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e57813b2-aef4-55f9-8eb7-a5039e709215" :question/math-academy-id "q-159574" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)={2}^{x+2y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={2}^{x+2y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)={2}^{x+h+2y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59c3f441-0499-575c-af10-b597d61e6e35" :knowledge-point/title "Partial Derivatives as Limits of Difference Quotients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e166b5-fcf7-5356-b265-a9ddb6c25684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(xh+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316573} {:answer/id #uuid "953efe5e-54c2-5d9d-a263-56e73f7599c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x-h+3y)+\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316574} {:answer/id #uuid "98a85703-86b1-5e13-b109-80748ace2883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{h\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316575} {:answer/id #uuid "5227559c-34b5-5cdc-9bcb-9917281b63df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316576} {:answer/id #uuid "1be9ab57-bbcb-5a14-abfe-b1d21331dcdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be9ab57-bbcb-5a14-abfe-b1d21331dcdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316577} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a1e004-7421-595f-baa8-8083abf52b65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50983d52-cea1-58fb-9d1c-99ed79226c46" :question/math-academy-id "q-159579" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d563e186-6da0-52b0-bd08-cde35c49f5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316580} {:answer/id #uuid "36326366-e9d9-51ca-a920-8eda10f515c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316581} {:answer/id #uuid "4df1f15d-897a-52aa-9ecd-9da536e2c2ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316582} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc985d9-e589-5b8f-9e06-aeb0e64df5fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316583} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8135fd-0ca3-5b70-ab1b-9ccdad130fc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36326366-e9d9-51ca-a920-8eda10f515c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316581} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab8ea4e-2381-5789-addf-372771f8a602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f1184a72-86fc-5f00-a377-62e4c111ae08" :question/math-academy-id "q-159585" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy,$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\pi  \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59c3f441-0499-575c-af10-b597d61e6e35" :knowledge-point/title "Partial Derivatives as Limits of Difference Quotients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bf7e9e6-aa44-546d-84b7-0b506abe0482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y-h+2)^{3}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316587} {:answer/id #uuid "6f884bf7-3a16-5527-ba28-541f19f7a567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316588} {:answer/id #uuid "539c13d5-f647-5aa7-a70f-1c8a8cc80ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{(x+h)^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316589} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b0461b-b881-5b1f-9a50-f11f0c727f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{(x+h)^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316590} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d6b307-307e-5957-872d-ef22a5b68eb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2h)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f884bf7-3a16-5527-ba28-541f19f7a567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316588} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d3f2fa6-fe32-532e-b60a-0e2d2b878fc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c099294e-ee23-53f7-9025-3261edeefbce" :question/math-academy-id "q-159589" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59c3f441-0499-575c-af10-b597d61e6e35" :knowledge-point/title "Partial Derivatives as Limits of Difference Quotients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84b701af-c529-5b05-b456-0e06b64d53fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{xy+h}-{3}^{xy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316594} {:answer/id #uuid "b2144579-7a42-528c-885f-bc7595f4eaf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y-h)}+{3}^{xy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316595} {:answer/id #uuid "56d1ab59-3fe5-5422-843e-e9faaa7a926c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{xy-h}+{3}^{xy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316596} {:answer/id #uuid "29eb0f3c-13e0-59de-89b9-911b9b5a4cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{xyh}-{3}^{xy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316597} {:answer/id #uuid "08367cc5-f1b1-59dd-9d90-f0a38eac0e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08367cc5-f1b1-59dd-9d90-f0a38eac0e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316598} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc32cc3-4cce-5480-af11-4bd33369076d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49dd5df0-89db-5a5b-9918-53b5f7fe906a" :question/math-academy-id "q-159593" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)={3}^{xy},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={3}^{xy},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)={3}^{x(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59c3f441-0499-575c-af10-b597d61e6e35" :knowledge-point/title "Partial Derivatives as Limits of Difference Quotients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65076698-65da-5d6d-ad89-556300fddc3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316601} {:answer/id #uuid "06c562d7-527e-5dc0-ae32-8154a09f19af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-yh}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316602} {:answer/id #uuid "86dd27ae-f2c4-58c0-b6ca-7d10fcc23510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y-h)}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316603} {:answer/id #uuid "74227c1d-9543-5902-9695-1a16b6e2eb45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{h\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316604} {:answer/id #uuid "46d2c71a-c714-5866-91ed-a05d6b0ad206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-yh}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65076698-65da-5d6d-ad89-556300fddc3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316601} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b0cc16d-b577-5417-8e31-9b3e8e192cab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e3d61b1-3a4f-5393-824a-d18cb80101e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-159594" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ec4c23-306d-5282-bd15-c90a84a2cd77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316608} {:answer/id #uuid "d369b486-2ffd-5109-8f0c-5ddf396492e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316609} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6c694f-090e-5927-9dcd-fdc9367b9a12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316610} {:answer/id #uuid "cbcdb296-8117-5213-bdfa-d455bcf548f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316611} {:answer/id #uuid "3b098e05-9104-5421-8989-7970deaa425b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbcdb296-8117-5213-bdfa-d455bcf548f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316611} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a157c6-b581-5834-87a8-1c652b4dc188" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "247ff6b4-cfa5-589a-92ee-337377d6bd3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-159597" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-2y\\sqrt{x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,e).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-2y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})-2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\cdot (3{x}^{2})-2y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,e)} & =3\\cdot {1}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\frac{e}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =3-e\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daccc790-7f79-570b-b129-00cbe32f3d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316615} {:answer/id #uuid "b527e5ca-c325-5f9c-92ac-a30e84694839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316616} {:answer/id #uuid "24161292-d0ce-5d89-a581-fa63fa194ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316617} {:answer/id #uuid "a6dd857d-6ffc-53da-a31f-9aefc3c97a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316618} {:answer/id #uuid "245b39f9-d671-5a4d-85ed-460eb1fa7fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "245b39f9-d671-5a4d-85ed-460eb1fa7fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316619} :answer-field/id #uuid "619af242-6a1e-5034-8f47-289c8e7bdfd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00bfed32-600a-58a8-8ea5-69052d463a56" :question/math-academy-id "q-159599" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{x}^{7}y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{x}^{7}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{7}y) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+{x}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{y})+{x}^{7}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{y}+{x}^{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,\\frac{1}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1/2)} & =\\frac{{e}^{1}}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+{1}^{7} \\\\  & =2e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2cf9ca2-1c18-5f6b-a1fb-7bc8e7e0f97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316622} {:answer/id #uuid "c069a1c5-3593-5dc1-9943-107b76a94416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316623} {:answer/id #uuid "6c7f6e4a-bb01-5571-a710-b20be5a112fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316624} {:answer/id #uuid "f74a4074-8c91-5cd0-975f-853eb7053b8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316625} {:answer/id #uuid "5b8b3741-8173-58d6-b130-4507e7751712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c069a1c5-3593-5dc1-9943-107b76a94416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316623} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4252601-24c6-56bc-a24a-d2dbe38e9de0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b93515d7-933b-5667-83d6-82023485db97" :question/math-academy-id "q-159602" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=4y{x}^{2}-x{y}^{4},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y{x}^{2}-x{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}\\cdot (1)-x\\cdot (4{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-4x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,1)} & =4\\cdot {2}^{2}-4\\cdot 2\\cdot {1}^{3} \\\\  & =16-8 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85265f94-96ca-55c4-b29a-1fff07b9876c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316629} {:answer/id #uuid "c915c857-4aa5-57b3-a5ae-26f238ebe537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316630} {:answer/id #uuid "0a7bc5ea-53ea-57c7-bfe5-b72cc7de25fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316631} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a6c5e1-6820-516d-ae49-9649741d2dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316632} {:answer/id #uuid "6625dd20-5905-51c5-b52c-ecad29453cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6a6c5e1-6820-516d-ae49-9649741d2dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316632} :answer-field/id #uuid "feddb534-ffa7-503c-bdcf-649194d54d6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "486530c9-71ac-574e-98a1-00908a232a97" :question/math-academy-id "q-159607" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y+{x}^{4}y,$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y+{x}^{4}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡y)+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y)+{x}^{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1+4 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Two-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "357125ad-3833-5f2f-926a-e5a44a0e170b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316636} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8d7054-d04e-5335-a7aa-415ec9ac968e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316637} {:answer/id #uuid "1c4dae83-9ebe-50c0-91b5-68c84348003d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316638} {:answer/id #uuid "5174d346-0e3a-5cee-9873-ebf98d7e5922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316639} {:answer/id #uuid "d87252ae-4943-5414-be8e-94dc4faa77fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed8d7054-d04e-5335-a7aa-415ec9ac968e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316637} :answer-field/id #uuid "037335cf-bdfb-5fbe-b72c-9551145780ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f5d5fa7-fec7-5274-8185-e140fc19c6ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-159613" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ given that $f(x,y)=xy+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot 1+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Two-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bcc28d4-64ec-5e54-9854-8ba7506bba72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316643} {:answer/id #uuid "3f941232-9522-5325-8d15-441dc304b3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316644} {:answer/id #uuid "0ef9d06f-1807-5112-ac9f-aadaeb55820c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316645} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed2b6eb-a902-5d6c-92de-6bab00cf4774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316646} {:answer/id #uuid "04ad9455-4c0f-533e-8e61-5a73f57e22f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed2b6eb-a902-5d6c-92de-6bab00cf4774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316646} :answer-field/id #uuid "f69e0f55-7b6c-5707-b70f-297b3d627586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9cfd495-d6cb-55e4-9b5a-eaa7955c1d75" :question/math-academy-id "q-159616" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ given that $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot (1)-y\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Two-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e0cdff-fa61-5f7d-a4a3-bc49f775d199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316650} {:answer/id #uuid "b3716e1b-8b5e-53e5-841a-46fd58d79639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-16y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316651} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c2071f-62e7-5140-8804-873d2d70b616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316652} {:answer/id #uuid "c6cd2eea-0fbc-50dd-b35d-f19a54f43133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316653} {:answer/id #uuid "9c929630-1715-53c8-bc4a-2dd65e872c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-16y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0e0cdff-fa61-5f7d-a4a3-bc49f775d199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316650} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf634820-a0bd-5357-baa7-ac1d13b2431e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84e45fe6-0b31-5027-8855-f065bf6bccdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-159619" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-8{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-8{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-8{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Two-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "661162e3-29b9-5070-b602-c9c69283e4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316657} {:answer/id #uuid "2858e9c6-24c1-5ffa-b291-f2cde0251007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2x+3y}+6x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316658} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6be4b-f538-5142-84d1-c091ce15b534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{2x+3y}+6x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316659} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ddf655-5d7e-508e-a62b-dd839ad9c805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316660} {:answer/id #uuid "f1773c6a-09ba-52cb-8b51-2b9cf26c9154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2x+3y}+2x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0ddf655-5d7e-508e-a62b-dd839ad9c805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316660} :answer-field/id #uuid "689057ca-6f2e-52a3-a9d7-194165093b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfa081e6-eae3-55c1-8810-551ff3bada92" :question/math-academy-id "q-159623" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={e}^{2x+3y}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum rule for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x+3y}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x}\\cdot {e}^{3y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{3}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{3y})+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 3{e}^{3y}+{x}^{2}\\cdot 3{y}^{2} \\\\  & =3{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Two-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "978084bc-6bf2-5803-95e5-58f403ea0aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}\\cos y + y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121925} {:answer/id #uuid "cbab19fd-3674-5c42-a736-5e4f8dc0491b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}\\cos y + x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121926} {:answer/id #uuid "ed0b169e-c044-5d32-b5d9-288aff4e2196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sin y + x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121927} {:answer/id #uuid "fd54039a-95ed-5699-9f0b-8d53d6d4493b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sin y + y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121928} {:answer/id #uuid "28025b94-e726-5b33-892c-5a7cf2fd7d40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y\\sin y + x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd54039a-95ed-5699-9f0b-8d53d6d4493b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sin y + y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121928} :answer-field/id #uuid "98d02875-fb45-5a92-a367-de0402e93596" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f09939e1-cd34-5f87-ba1b-e1ac2c9af5b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-35709" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\cdot (2x)+y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
